<article class="eva-page eva-squarespace-page">
  <section class="eva-page-hero" id="overview" aria-labelledby="sq-eva-title">
    <div class="eva-page-orbit" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="page-width eva-page-hero__grid">
      <div class="eva-page-hero__copy">
        <p class="kicker">EVA / A WE-Sensing venture</p>
        <h1 id="sq-eva-title">A familiar pad. A new layer of health insight.</h1>
        <p>EVA is a smart menstrual sensing pad under development, designed to measure selected biological changes in menstrual fluid through a product women already use.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-eva" href="#how-it-works">See How EVA Works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="eva-text-link" href="#partnerships">Explore Partnerships <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </div>
      <figure class="eva-product-stage eva-product-stage--render">
        <div class="eva-product-stage__label"><span>PRODUCT SYSTEM</span><span>CONCEPT VIEW</span></div>
        <img src="/assets/eva/eva-hero-product.webp" width="1823" height="863" alt="Concept render of the EVA smart sensing pad, detachable reusable reader, and application">
        <figcaption class="eva-product-stage__legend"><span><i></i>Sensing pad</span><span><i></i>Reusable electronics</span><span><i></i>Longitudinal view</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="page-width eva-hero-disclaimer"><span>Development status</span><p>EVA is currently under development and is not available for clinical diagnosis or treatment decisions.</p></div>
  </section>

  <nav class="eva-local-nav" aria-label="EVA page sections"><div class="page-width" data-eva-local-navigation></div></nav>

  <section class="eva-need section-pad" id="need" aria-labelledby="sq-eva-need-title">
    <div class="page-width">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="kicker">The need</p><h2 id="sq-eva-need-title">Important biological changes remain invisible between clinical visits.</h2></div><p>Wearable devices can reveal patterns in behavior and physiology, while clinical tests provide detailed information at individual moments. EVA is being developed to help capture selected biological changes during the time between those measurements.</p></div>
      <div class="eva-timeline" role="img" aria-label="Timeline showing EVA measurements between two clinical visits"><div class="eva-timeline__labels"><span>Clinical visit</span><span>Time between visits</span><span>Clinical visit</span></div><div class="eva-timeline__track"><i class="visit-node"></i><span><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><i class="visit-node"></i></div><div class="eva-timeline__caption"><span>Detailed measurement</span><strong>EVA longitudinal measurements</strong><span>Detailed measurement</span></div></div>
      <div class="eva-context-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Consumer wearables</h3><p>Can help reveal behavioral and physiological patterns through indirect signals.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Clinical testing</h3><p>Provides detailed information at individual moments under clinical direction.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>EVA’s intended role</h3><p>Explore longitudinal biological information between visits without replacing either approach.</p></article></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="eva-product-design section-pad" id="product-design" aria-labelledby="sq-eva-product-title">
    <div class="page-width"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="kicker">Product design</p><h2 id="sq-eva-product-title">Designed around a product women already know.</h2></div><p>The EVA concept combines a disposable sensing pad, a detachable reader, and an application intended to organize measurements over time.</p></div><div class="eva-component-intro"><article><span>01</span><h3>Smart Sensing Pad</h3><p>A familiar disposable pad containing an integrated sensing region.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Reusable Reader</h3><p>A detachable electronic device that captures and transfers sensor signals.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>EVA Application</h3><p>A secure interface intended to organize measurements and present longitudinal trends.</p></article></div>
      <div class="eva-product-gallery">
        <article class="eva-gallery-card eva-gallery-card--front"><div class="eva-gallery-card__meta"><span>01</span><h3>Pad front view</h3></div><img class="eva-gallery-image eva-gallery-image--pad" src="/assets/eva/eva-pad.png" alt="Front view of the EVA sensing pad"></article>
        <article class="eva-gallery-card eva-gallery-card--back"><div class="eva-gallery-card__meta"><span>02</span><h3>Pad rear view</h3></div><img class="eva-gallery-image eva-gallery-image--pad" src="/assets/eva/eva-pad-back.png" alt="Rear view of the EVA sensing pad"></article>
        <article class="eva-gallery-card eva-gallery-card--exploded"><div class="eva-gallery-card__meta"><span>03</span><h3>Exploded layer view</h3></div><img class="eva-gallery-image eva-gallery-image--layer" src="/assets/eva/sensing-layer.png" alt="EVA sensing-layer architecture"></article>
        <article class="eva-gallery-card eva-gallery-card--reader"><div class="eva-gallery-card__meta"><span>04</span><h3>Detachable reader</h3></div><img class="eva-gallery-image" src="/assets/eva/logger-detach.png" alt="Detachable EVA reader"></article>
        <article class="eva-gallery-card eva-gallery-card--kit"><div class="eva-gallery-card__meta"><span>05</span><h3>Starter kit</h3></div><img class="eva-gallery-image" src="/assets/eva/starterkit.png" alt="EVA starter kit"></article>
        <article class="eva-gallery-card eva-gallery-card--app"><div class="eva-gallery-card__meta"><span>06</span><h3>Application interface</h3></div><img class="eva-gallery-image eva-gallery-image--application" src="/assets/eva/application.png" alt="EVA application interface"></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="eva-how section-pad" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="sq-eva-how-title">
    <div class="page-width"><div class="section-heading"><p class="kicker">How it works</p><h2 id="sq-eva-how-title">From routine use to a longitudinal view.</h2></div><ol class="eva-how-grid"><li><span>01</span><h3>Use</h3><p>The pad is worn as part of the user’s normal menstrual routine.</p></li><li><span>02</span><h3>Sense</h3><p>Integrated electrochemical sensors interact with menstrual fluid and generate electrical signals.</p></li><li><span>03</span><h3>Interpret</h3><p>The reusable reader and data-processing system organize and analyze the sensor response.</p></li><li><span>04</span><h3>Understand</h3><p>The application presents longitudinal trends intended to support future health understanding and clinical research.</p></li></ol></div>
  </section>

  <section class="eva-technology-page section-pad" id="eva-technology" aria-labelledby="sq-eva-tech-title">
    <div class="page-width"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="kicker">Technology</p><h2 id="sq-eva-tech-title">Advanced sensing, integrated into a familiar form.</h2></div><p>EVA extends WE-Sensing’s broader sensing platform into a women’s health application while keeping the product and user experience central to the system design.</p></div>
      <div class="eva-tech-layout"><div class="eva-tech-architecture"><img class="eva-tech-architecture__image" src="/assets/eva/eva-concept.png" alt="EVA technology architecture from sensing interface to longitudinal interpretation"></div>
        <div class="eva-tech-modules"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Electrochemical Sensing Interface</h3><p>Flexible sensor elements designed to respond to selected chemical changes in menstrual fluid.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Integrated Fluid Interaction</h3><p>A sensing region positioned within the pad architecture to interact with collected menstrual fluid.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Reusable Electronics</h3><p>A detachable reader designed to acquire signals from the disposable sensing pad.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Signal Interpretation</h3><p>Data-processing methods intended to transform complex sensor responses into longitudinal measurements and interpretable trends.</p></div></article></div>
      </div>
      <div class="eva-capabilities" aria-label="Related WE-Sensing expertise"><span>Electrochemical sensing</span><span>Sensor materials</span><span>Custom electronics</span><span>Signal processing</span><span>Machine learning</span><span>Scalable fabrication</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="eva-development section-pad" id="development" aria-labelledby="sq-eva-development-title">
    <div class="page-width"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="kicker">Development</p><h2 id="sq-eva-development-title">A staged path from sensing feasibility to future launch.</h2></div><p>The sequence below describes the intended development path. Individual stage status will be published only after formal project review.</p></div><ol class="eva-roadmap" data-eva-roadmap></ol><div class="eva-development-disclaimer"><span>Important</span><p>EVA is currently under development and is not available for clinical diagnosis or treatment decisions.</p></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="eva-partnerships section-pad" id="partnerships" aria-labelledby="sq-eva-partnership-title">
    <div class="page-width eva-partnerships__grid"><div><p class="kicker">Partnerships</p><h2 id="sq-eva-partnership-title">Building EVA with scientific and clinical partners.</h2><p>WE-Sensing welcomes focused conversations with teams whose expertise can help shape rigorous research, product development, and responsible translation.</p><a class="button button-eva" href="/?inquiry=eva#contact">Discuss an EVA Partnership <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><ul class="eva-partnership-list" data-eva-partnerships></ul></div>
  </section>
  <aside class="eva-footer-disclaimer" aria-label="EVA development disclaimer"><div class="page-width"><span>EVA development status</span><p>EVA is currently under development and is not available for clinical diagnosis or treatment decisions.</p></div></aside>
